  "asr_text": "He was not mad, the old man's housemate insisted, only nervous. His illness had sharpened his senses, especially his hearing. He heard everything in heaven and earth. Surely that proved he was sane. His listeners should judge how calmly he told the story. He loved the old man, who had never hurt him. He wanted no money. But that pale blue eye, covered by a thin film, like a vulture's, made his blood turn cold. He would kill the old man and close it forever. For seven nights, at midnight, he eased open the bedroom door. Slowly, he slipped his head inside with a covered lantern. He let one thin ray fall across the eye, always closed. He could do nothing. He hated the eye, not the man. Each morning, he greeted his housemate warmly.",
